#heading(level: 3, numbering: none)[Elementary row operations.]
<elementary-row-operations.>
All elementry row operations can be applied to a matrix. You can think
of a matrix as just a short-hand way of writing a system of linear
equations. \
Since systems of linear equations sometimes take several steps to solve,
it is important to write each operation you use along the way. \
Use a matrix to solve this system:

$ 2 x & - 2 y & + 3 z & = & 9\
- x & + 3 y &  & = & - 3\
2 x & - 5 y & + 5 z & = & 17 $

